  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Friday)\nIssued at 1232 PM MDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nCurrent upper air models show mild ridge over the far western\nCONUS, with trough over the Great Lakes region, and northwest flow\nover the forecast area. Surface analysis depicts high pressure\nover the Dakotas, with a low over south central MT. Winds are\nrelatively light and variable this afternoon. Skies are clear \nwith temperatures currently in the 70s to low 80s. \n\nWinds will slowly transition to out of the southeast as we\nprogress through the afternoon, as the surface high slides east of\nthe forecast area, with dry and mild conditions continuing the \nrest of today. Strengthening Low Level Jet tonight will increase \nchances for precipitation in the overnight hours, mainly over \nsouth-central SD. MU CAPE values in the 1500-2000 j/Kg range, \nalong with steepening lapse rates and shear in the 35-45kt range \nwill support chances for elevated strong storms with hail \npotential between around 09-14Z Saturday morning. \n\nHotter temperatures return for Saturday and Sunday, with \nhighs in the 90s to possibly low 100s. Upper ridge flattens out a\nbit towards Sunday, bringing more quasi-zonal flow. Expect\ntemperatures to cool a bit by Monday through the rest of next\nweek. Low level southeasterly flow will be common next week,\nbringing increasing moisture into the region. Expect more active \nweather potential next week, with daily chances for at least \nisolated showers/storms",
